From c83c23dd40de4dbdadf43886d116096cb2ada1c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MastaG <mastag@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:01:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] tools: kytyps5-run.sh starts Kyty with --hdr when gamescope
 outputs HDR, with the gamescope WSI layer that offers the HDR10 formats

With Steam's HDR on, gamescope sends HDR10 to the display, but Kyty ran in
SDR: the wrapper passed no --hdr, so the game was told SDR and its picture
was shown as SDR inside the HDR signal. The wrapper now reads gamescope's
GAMESCOPE_DISPLAY_HDR_ENABLED on the root display and then passes --hdr.

The HDR10 swapchain formats on gamescope's Xwayland come from the gamescope
WSI layer, which needs ENABLE_GAMESCOPE_WSI=1 and gamescope's own Wayland
socket. Steam gives a game both; with Steam stopped this unit has neither,
so the socket name is read from gamescope-session's environment file
($XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/gamescope-environment). Without a socket name nothing
changes, since the layer without one stops the start with its "Hooking has
failed" dialog.

Checked on a BC-250 (CachyOS, gamescope 3.17, Mesa RADV), surface colour
spaces from vulkaninfo on gamescope's Xwayland:
- no layer: SRGB_NONLINEAR only (Kyty stays SDR, as before)
- layer: also HDR10_ST2084, EXTENDED_SRGB_LINEAR, PASS_THROUGH; DXVK_HDR
  makes no difference
ASTRO BOT then runs with an A2B10G10R10 swapchain in HDR10_ST2084. Steam's
HDR off: the property is 0 and the start is unchanged. On KDE, --hdr alone
gives HDR10 (PQ) over Wayland; that path goes through the launcher's own
HDR setting and is not touched here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012SzrKGFxZe6chpS3Qx81Z7
---
 tools/kytyps5-native/kytyps5-run.sh | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/kytyps5-native/kytyps5-run.sh b/tools/kytyps5-native/kytyps5-run.sh
index 4597ee1..1f96f0d 100755
--- a/tools/kytyps5-native/kytyps5-run.sh
+++ b/tools/kytyps5-native/kytyps5-run.sh
@@ -132,13 +132,27 @@ done
 	notice "KytyPS5-Native update available" "$(head -1 "$CONFIG/update-available"): update it in the Decky plugin"
 [ -n "$NOTICE_TITLES" ] && export KYTY_NOTICE_TITLE="$NOTICE_TITLES" KYTY_NOTICE_TEXT="$NOTICE_TEXTS"
 
+# HDR: when gamescope outputs HDR (Steam's display setting), Kyty gets an HDR10 swapchain. With Steam
+# stopped, the gamescope WSI layer (which offers the HDR10 formats) is asked for here; Kyty falls back
+# to SDR when the surface offers no HDR10 format.
+HDR_ARGS=
+if [ "$(DISPLAY=$ROOT_DISPLAY xprop -root GAMESCOPE_DISPLAY_HDR_ENABLED 2>/dev/null | awk '{print $NF}')" = 1 ]; then
+	# The layer talks to gamescope over its own Wayland socket: Steam gives a game its name, this
+	# unit (Steam stopped) reads it where gamescope-session leaves its environment.
+	: "${GAMESCOPE_WAYLAND_DISPLAY:=$(sed -n 's/^GAMESCOPE_WAYLAND_DISPLAY=//p' \
+		"${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR:-/run/user/$(id -u)}/gamescope-environment" 2>/dev/null)}"
+	if [ -n "$GAMESCOPE_WAYLAND_DISPLAY" ]; then
+		HDR_ARGS=--hdr
+		export ENABLE_GAMESCOPE_WSI=1 GAMESCOPE_WAYLAND_DISPLAY
+	fi
+fi
 MARKER=$SHARE/data/.exit-$TITLE
 rm -f "$MARKER" "$VIDEO_FLAG"
 front "$GAME_APPID"
 {
 	echo "== $(date) $GAME"
 	SDL_JOYSTICK_ALLOW_BACKGROUND_EVENTS=1 KYTY_EXIT_MARKER="$MARKER" KYTY_GAMESCOPE_APPID=$GAME_APPID "$EMU" --game "$GAME" \
-		--screen-width "${SCREEN%x*}" --screen-height "${SCREEN#*x}" --fullscreen --no-splash --skip-notice-screen
+		--screen-width "${SCREEN%x*}" --screen-height "${SCREEN#*x}" --fullscreen --no-splash --skip-notice-screen $HDR_ARGS
 	echo "== exit=$?"
 } >> "$LOG" 2>&1 &
 EMUPID=$!
